      "text": "We fetched a bunch of potentially interesting posts and passed them to the scorer. That layer is called Retrieval. \nThen the Scorer we have does a lightweight heuristics based ordering.  How can we make this better?\n\n1. We can use models here for Ranking. A model is just a math equation. It is made of code and data. It processes the input through the equation and produces an output.\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 16.228596831774485,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "We fetched a bunch of potentially interesting posts and passed them to the scorer. That layer is called Retrieval. \nThen the Scorer we have does a lightweight heuristics based ordering.  How can we make this better?\n\n1. We can use models here for Ranking. A model is just a math equation. It is made of code and data. It processes the input through the equation and produces an output.\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
