    },
    {
      "id": "MANsgYXk3bGgLSBGr29mB",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2426.986595959146,
      "y": 11114.661860165994,
      "width": 124.62387084960938,
      "height": 40,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b8S",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 723391748,
      "version": 312,
      "versionNonce": 2099224380,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1782325574987,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "for serving with\nlive/latest data",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "for serving with\nlive/latest data",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "vQsbBNcZHBYoD60P7eP_J",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 41.039363971369085,
      "y": 8225.709300387294,
      "width": 1845.135009765625,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b8T",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1418059012,
      "version": 1620,
      "versionNonce": 1306332932,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1782326839612,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. A model is as good as the data it's trained on. So maintaining data and feature quality is top priority.\n2. In the previous setup, data fetch is not coordinated. If training and serving start using mismatched data (eg. trained on num_likes_7day, served on num_likes_1day), quality will silently deteriorate.\n3. So we need a central registry to define what a feature is, how it's computed, who uses it, versions of it used by different models etc.\n4. We also introduce API to hide the complexity of computing features behind this and expose simple calls to get live features and exact time-point training features. (e.g num_likes when a user actually clicked a post, not current value)\n5. This includes additional monitoring to avoid the dreaded issues with drift where features start acting different between training and serving. (e.g. feature definition mismatch, pipeline faults etc.)",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. A model is as good as the data it's trained on. So maintaining data and feature quality is top priority.\n2. In the previous setup, data fetch is not coordinated. If training and serving start using mismatched data (eg. trained on num_likes_7day, served on num_likes_1day), quality will silently deteriorate.\n3. So we need a central registry to define what a feature is, how it's computed, who uses it, versions of it used by different models etc.\n4. We also introduce API to hide the complexity of computing features behind this and expose simple calls to get live features and exact time-point training features. (e.g num_likes when a user actually clicked a post, not current value)\n5. This includes additional monitoring to avoid the dreaded issues with drift where features start acting different between training and serving. (e.g. feature definition mismatch, pipeline faults etc.)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
